.TH WALLACE 1 "November 2026" "wallace 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wallace \- forensic token usage and USD cost auditor for Antigravity IDE and CLI brains
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wallace
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-help\fR | \fB\-\-help\-all\fR | \fB\-\-version\fR]
.br
.B wallace report
[\fBsummary\fR|\fBprojects\fR|\fBfeatures\fR|\fBconversations\fR|\fBmodels\fR|\fBsources\fR|\fBdaily\fR|\fBweekly\fR|\fBmonthly\fR|\fBinterval\fR]
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B wallace task
\fITASK_ID\fR [\fB\-\-project\fR \fISLUG\fR] [\fB\-\-conversation\fR \fIUUID\fR]... [\fB\-\-include\-qa\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR \fBtable\fR|\fBjson\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR \fIPATH\fR]
.br
.B wallace conversation show
\fICONVERSATION_ID\fR [\fB\-\-turns\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR \fIPATH\fR]
.br
.B wallace query
\fICONVERSATION_ID\fR [\fB\-\-turns\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR \fIPATH\fR]
.br
.B wallace visidata
[\fBopen\fR|\fBconfig\fR|\fBinstall\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B wallace config
[\fBshow\fR|\fBinit\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR]
.br
.B wallace metrics
[\fBexport\fR|\fBserve\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B wallace schema
[\fB\-\-list\fR | \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR \fBjson\-schema\fR|\fBcsvw\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR \fIPATH\fR]
.br
.B wallace install
[\fB\-\-bin\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Named after Oscar Wallace, the Treasury accountant who followed the ledger in
\fIThe Untouchables\fR, \fBwallace\fR audits Antigravity IDE
(\fI~/.gemini/antigravity\fR) and Antigravity CLI (\fI~/.gemini/antigravity-cli\fR)
brain directories. It resolves canonical \fI<PROJECT>\-WP\-<NN>\fR identifiers
from git branches, worker names, titles, and initial prompt briefs, and
aggregates uncached input, cached input, thinking, and output tokens alongside
estimated USD spend across timeframes, projects, tasks, conversations, and models.
.PP
\fBwallace\fR integrates directly with \fBVisiData\fR (\fBvd\fR) via flat typed
JSONL streams, TSV/CSV tables, multi-sheet SQLite ledgers, and an installable
VisiData plugin defining currency formatting, sum aggregators, and quick
frequency shortcuts.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B report summary|projects|features|conversations|models|sources|daily|weekly|monthly|interval
Aggregate token usage and USD spend across projects, features, and timeframes.
Combine any report verb with \fB\-\-period day|week|month|interval\fR and
\fB\-\-interval\fR (for example \fB6h\fR, \fB7d\fR, \fB14d\fR).
.TP
.B task \fITASK_ID\fR
Aggregate all conversations matching \fITASK_ID\fR (including project-scoped
bare \fIWP\-NN\fR fallbacks, explicit \fB\-\-conversation\fR UUIDs, and optional
prorated QA attribution via \fB\-\-include\-qa\fR) as an aligned table or
Draft 2020-12 JSON (\fItask\-usage.schema.json\fR).
.TP
.B conversation show \fIID\fR / query \fIID\fR
Query a single conversation UUID (or unambiguous prefix) and return self,
subagent, and combined token usage and USD cost as JSON.
.TP
.B visidata open|config|install
Launch VisiData with a multi-sheet Wallace SQLite workbook (or specific sheet),
print the Wallace VisiData plugin snippet, or install it into \fI~/.visidata/\fR.
.TP
.B config show|init
Print active configuration or write an editable default TOML pricing config.
.TP
.B metrics export|serve
Emit Prometheus exposition metrics or run an HTTP \fI/metrics\fR exporter.
.TP
.B schema
List or emit JSON Schema Draft 2020-12 and W3C CSVW data-interchange contracts
(\fBtoken\-report\fR, \fBledger\-row\fR, \fBconversation\-usage\fR, and \fBtask\-usage\fR).
.TP
.B install
Install an executable \fBwallace\fR launcher shim into \fB\-\-bin\-dir\fR or
\fI${WALLACE_BIN_DIR:\-~/.local/bin}/wallace\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WALLACE_CONFIG
Path to TOML configuration file (default: \fI~/.config/wallace/config.toml\fR).
.TP
.B WALLACE_IDE_DIR, WALLACE_CLI_DIR, WALLACE_BRAIN_DIRS
Override Antigravity IDE, CLI, and standalone brain directories.
.TP
.B WALLACE_BIN_DIR
Override target directory for \fBwallace install\fR (default: \fI~/.local/bin\fR).
.TP
.B WALLACE_METRICS_HOST, WALLACE_METRICS_PORT
Override bind address and TCP port for \fBwallace metrics serve\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime, lookup, validation, or file error.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid CLI argument or flag.
